  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 15,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.74,
            0.047,
            0.862,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Quadrilaterals"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.086,
            0.847,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Deduction 6— What can we say about the angles of a parallelogram?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.117,
            0.823,
            0.138
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the parallelogram ABCD, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { A B }   |   |   \\mathrm { C D } |"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , and AD is a transversal to them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.147,
            0.497,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A} + \\angle \\mathrm{D} = 180^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (sum of the internal angles on the same side of a transversal)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.203,
            0.284,
            0.22
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.221,
            0.461,
            0.239
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{D}=180-\\angle \\mathrm{A}=180-30=150^{\\circ}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.24,
            0.503,
            0.277
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Similarly, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { A D }   |   |   \\mathrm { B C } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and AB and CD are transversals to them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.507,
            0.142,
            0.931,
            0.271
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.507,
                0.142,
                0.931,
                0.271
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_8.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.415,
            0.287,
            0.606,
            0.307
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{S}0,\\angle \\mathrm{A}+\\angle \\mathrm{B}=180^{\\circ}."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.415,
            0.317,
            0.607,
            0.336
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{S}0,\\angle \\mathrm{C}+\\angle \\mathrm{D}=180^{\\circ}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.34,
            0.673,
            0.362
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using these equations, we get "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{B} = 150^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle C = 30^{\\circ}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.37,
            0.835,
            0.409
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We see that in this parallelogram, the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "adjacent pairs of angles add up to 180° and opposite pairs of angles are equal.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.409,
            0.236,
            0.426
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.168,
            0.431,
            0.828,
            0.452
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A}+\\angle \\mathrm{B}=180^{\\circ},\\angle \\mathrm{A}+\\angle \\mathrm{D}=180^{\\circ},\\angle \\mathrm{C}+\\angle \\mathrm{D}=180^{\\circ},\\mathrm{and}\\angle \\mathrm{B}+\\angle \\mathrm{C}=180^{\\circ}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.456,
            0.204,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "And,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.386,
            0.48,
            0.612,
            0.499
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_16.jpg",
          "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{A} = \\angle \\mathrm{C}, \\mathrm{and} \\angle \\mathrm{B} = \\angle \\mathrm{D}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.515,
            0.838,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since the adjacent angles are the interior angles on the same side of a transversal to a pair of parallel lines, they must add up to 180°."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.556,
            0.847,
            0.578
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? What about the opposite angles? Will they be equal in all parallelograms?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.576,
            0.424,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If yes, how can we be sure?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.599,
            0.505,
            0.618
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us take one of the angles to be x."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.618,
            0.421,
            0.636
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What are the other angles?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.636,
            0.362,
            0.654
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{P} + \\angle \\mathrm{R} = 180^{\\circ}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.655,
            0.385,
            0.672
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_23.jpg",
          "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{R} = 180 - \\angle \\mathrm{P} = 180 - x."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.673,
            0.458,
            0.691
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_24.jpg",
          "content": "Similarly, since   \\angle \\mathrm{A} + \\angle \\mathrm{R} = 180^{\\circ},"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.692,
            0.605,
            0.71
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_15_equation_25.jpg",
          "content": "\\angle A = 180 - \\angle R = 180 - (180 - x) = 180 - 180 + x = x."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.711,
            0.332,
            0.728
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{P} = \\angle \\mathrm{A} = x."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 27,
          "bbox": [
            0.608,
            0.583,
            0.899,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 27,
              "bbox": [
                0.608,
                0.583,
                0.899,
                0.726
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_27.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 28,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.729,
            0.624,
            0.747
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Similarly, we can deduce that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{R} = \\angle \\mathrm{E} = 180 - x."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 29,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.747,
            0.847,
            0.785
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, this shows that "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "the opposite angles of a parallelogram are always equal.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 30,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.794,
            0.845,
            0.816
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Deduction 7— What can we say about the sides of a parallelogram?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 31,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.825,
            0.848,
            0.862
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "By looking at a parallelogram, it appears that the opposite sides are equal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 32,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.862,
            0.848,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can we again use congruence to show this? Which two triangles can be considered for this?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 33,
          "bbox": [
            0.877,
            0.915,
            0.912,
            0.936
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "97"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
